course: dictionary
lesson: 15500
title: Stutter: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A stutter is when speech comes out in sudden stops or repeated first sounds, like «b-b-ball». The person does not mean to do it. Some people have a stutter for a long time, and it is a difference in how they speak, not a sign that they are nervous or less clever.
explain: «Maya has a stutter, so she sometimes needs a moment to get her words out.» The clue is in the words that follow: she needs a moment. So stutter means a way of speaking with stops and repeats. Try your meaning in the sentence: it still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: The same word works for machines. «The old bus began to stutter up the steep hill.» A bus cannot speak, so stutter must mean something else here: it runs in short, uneven bursts. The clues are old, steep and up the hill, which suggest a struggling engine.
explain: When you hear someone who stutters, be patient and let them finish. Speech therapists help people who stutter, and that is a job you can learn about too.
fact: To stutter is to speak with sudden stops or by repeating the first sounds of words, like «b-b-ball», without meaning to.
fact: A stutter is this way of speaking, which some people have for a long time.
fact: An engine or machine stutters when it runs in short, uneven bursts.
fact: A stutter is a speech difference, not a sign of being nervous or less clever.
fact: Speech therapists help people who stutter. Be patient and let the person finish their sentence.
exercise: «The old bus began to stutter up the steep hill.» What does stutter mean here? | Sang a happy tune | Glowed brightly in the dark | *Moved in short, jerky bursts | Stopped and was never fixed again
exercise: «Maya has a stutter, so she sometimes needs a moment to get her words out.» Which statement is true? | A stutter only happens when you tell a joke | *A stutter is a speech difference, not a sign of being unclever | A stutter means you are being rude on purpose | A stutter means you are too lazy to speak
exercise: Find and copy the word that means spoke with sudden stops in «He stuttered on the first word, then finished the sentence.» | first | *stuttered | finished | sentence
test: What is the best way to help someone who has a stutter? | Look away and finish their sentence for them | *Be patient and let them finish | Tell them to speak faster | Laugh so they feel better
test: Which sentence uses stutter as a noun, meaning the way of speaking? | The old engine began to stutter. | *Her stutter never stopped her from being a great storyteller. | He will stutter when he is nervous. | They stutter up the hill every day.
exam: Which job helps people who stutter? | *Speech therapist | Bus driver | Plumber | Baker
